{
    "uuid": "ec29ae9c-2551-480f-81f7-f230f6100951",
    "name": "SOC Triage",
    "description": "For an analyst working an alert queue, where a false positive costs more than a miss. It carries the shipped default's evidence weights, thresholds and bands unchanged, so the quality number a value is given here is the number every other profile on this instance gives it; what changes is what the page puts in front of you and how long it treats a report as current. TLP and false-positive are pinned, so the page states their absence rather than leaving a gap, and malware classification, threat actors and ATT&CK patterns sort ahead of everything else it draws. Shelf life is shortened to what triage acts on: thirty days for an address rather than ninety, three weeks for a URL rather than two months, because an answer about what is live now should stop being current quickly. It counts the same galaxies as an attribution as the shipped default. It runs nothing: the modules it names arrive ticked on the Enrichment tab and a run still takes a press, and a module an administrator has not turned on stays off. It is meant to be forked rather than edited - take a copy, change your own, and the nearest profile to the reader wins.",
